@startuml
title UML sequence behaviour — Build a digest
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
box "Backend — Popkin Application and Domain" #ECFDF3
  participant "DigestEmailComposer" as composer
  participant "DigestRules" as rules
  participant "NotificationLinks" as links
end box
box "Backend — Popkin Infrastructure" #FFF4E5
  database "Popkin database" as db
end box
composer -> rules : Period(previous digest, now, weekly)
rules --> composer : Since 6 pm yesterday, or last Sunday
composer -> db : Held changes in the period, with each change as it is now
db --> composer : Changes still standing
composer -> db : Unread Everyone messages by others, per Popkin not muted or Just for me
db --> composer : Counts
composer -> db : Own stories due within 2 days (Plan on, not Done); key dates within 2 days (RemindersOn)
db --> composer : Rows
composer -> rules : NeedsYou(stories, dates) (L2-165 AC2)
rules --> composer : Up to 5 rows, stories first
composer -> rules : OrderSections; PickLines; photos (AC3, AC4)
rules --> composer : Sections, most first; 3 lines; 4 photos; "and {n} messages"
composer -> rules : Subject(needs, changes, popkins, weekly)
rules --> composer : "Your day in Popkin: ..."
composer -> links : Open Popkin; Mute a Popkin; settings; unsubscribe (AC6)
links --> composer : URLs
composer --> composer : DigestEmailModel, or Nothing when no change is left
@enduml
